{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Resurgence.StokesConstantQDimCategoricity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Resurgence.StokesConstantQDimCategoricity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Coeff","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerCanonical"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.OrbitMagnitudesAreQDims.isQDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.OrbitMagnitudesAreQDims.isQDim","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/StokesConstantQDimCategoricity.lean#L172-L172","doc":"Each orbit magnitude is *some* quantum integer as a full `q`-series. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.OrbitMagnitudesAreQDims.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.OrbitMagnitudesAreQDims.mk","kind":"ctor","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/StokesConstantQDimCategoricity.lean#L170-L170","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.OrbitMagnitudesAreQDims","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.OrbitMagnitudesAreQDims","kind":"structure","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/StokesConstantQDimCategoricity.lean#L162-L172","doc":"**OPEN (bean `qou-nkm1`).**  Hypothesis that a family of bar-orbit Stokes\nmagnitudes `mag : ι → Polynomial ℤ` is a categorical q-dimension spectrum: each\nmagnitude coincides, *as a `q`-series* (not merely at the vacuous `q=1`), with a\nquantum-integer polynomial `[n(i)]_q`.  Deliberately **no instance** — the\nfigure-eight datum refutes the direct route (`stokesDesc_ne_qIntPoly`,\n`qIntThreePoly_ne_const_three`), so instantiating this would launder a refuted\nidentification.  Content-bearing: the field is a genuine `q`-series equality, not\n`True`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.stokesDesc_ne_qIntPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.stokesDesc_ne_qIntPoly","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/StokesConstantQDimCategoricity.lean#L147-L149","doc":"In particular the Stokes series is **not** any quantum integer `[n]_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.stokes_not_nonneg_combination","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.stokes_not_nonneg_combination","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/StokesConstantQDimCategoricity.lean#L135-L145","doc":"**Structural exclusion (scope-(b)).**  No polynomial with non-negative\ncoefficients equals the Stokes descendant series — because that series has\n`coeff₁ = −8 < 0`.  In particular **no categorical q-dimension, and no\n`ℕ`-combination of q-dimensions, is the Stokes series.**  This is the magnitude\nanalogue of the KL-positivity prune that excluded the *sign*. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.stokesDesc_coeff_one_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.stokesDesc_coeff_one_neg","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/StokesConstantQDimCategoricity.lean#L131-L133","doc":"**The Stokes series carries a negative coefficient:** `coeff₁ = −8`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.stokesDesc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.stokesDesc","kind":"def","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/StokesConstantQDimCategoricity.lean#L126-L129","doc":"The GGM `4₁` Stokes **descendant series** (leading terms, exact integers):\n`1 − 8q̃ − 9q̃² + 18q̃³ + 46q̃⁴`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.qIntPoly_coeff_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.qIntPoly_coeff_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/StokesConstantQDimCategoricity.lean#L120-L124","doc":"**Positivity invariant.**  Every coefficient of a quantum-integer polynomial\nis non-negative (indeed `∈ {0,1}`).  The categorical q-dimensions inherit this:\nthey are `ℕ`-combinations of such objects. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.qIntPoly_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.qIntPoly_coeff","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/StokesConstantQDimCategoricity.lean#L113-L118","doc":"Its `k`-th coefficient is `1` if `k < n`, else `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.qIntPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.qIntPoly","kind":"def","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/StokesConstantQDimCategoricity.lean#L110-L111","doc":"The quantum-integer polynomial `[n]_q = ∑_{i<n} qⁱ` over `ℤ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.qIntThreePoly_ne_const_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.qIntThreePoly_ne_const_three","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/StokesConstantQDimCategoricity.lean#L90-L96","doc":"**The match fails off `q = 1`.**  `[3]_q ≠ 3` as polynomials — the degree-1\ncoefficient is `1 ≠ 0`.  So the geometric Stokes constant `3` equals `[3]_q`\n*only* at the vacuous point `q = 1`, never as a `q`-series identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.qIntThreePoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.qIntThreePoly","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/StokesConstantQDimCategoricity.lean#L87-L88","doc":"`[3]_q` as a polynomial in `ℤ[q]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.qInt_three_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.qInt_three_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/StokesConstantQDimCategoricity.lean#L70-L73","doc":"The observed match `[3]_1 = 3`, exhibited as the **vacuous** `q=1`\ncoincidence (a special case of `qInt_at_one`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.qInt_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.qInt_three","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/StokesConstantQDimCategoricity.lean#L66-L68","doc":"`[3]_q = 1 + q + q²` — genuinely `q`-dependent (over any field). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.qInt_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.qInt_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/StokesConstantQDimCategoricity.lean#L59-L64","doc":"**`q = 1` quantum-integer spectrum is all of `ℕ`.**  `[n]_q|_{q=1} = n`.\nThis is the vacuity engine: since *every* natural number `n` equals `[n]_1`, a\nmatch \"integer `k` = `[k]_{q=1}`\" (as for the Stokes constant `3 = [3]_1`)\ncarries **no** categorical information — it holds for `8`, `46`, `90` alike. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.qInt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.qInt","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/StokesConstantQDimCategoricity.lean#L47-L51","doc":"The **quantum integer** `[n]_q = ∑_{i<n} qⁱ = 1 + q + ⋯ + q^{n-1}`.  Mirrors\nthe corpus `QOU.MathlibExt.qInt` (`QIntegerFactorial.lean`); reproduced locally\nso this refutation verifies against Mathlib alone. ","signatureChunk":0}]}